<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01736</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>3b82788f-a9ce-4c6a-b400-cfe4728e55fb</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para class="os-raise-text-bold"><emphasis>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</emphasis></para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Here are a few pairs of positive numbers whose sum is 50.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Row</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">First number</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Second number</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Product</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>a</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>49</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>b</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>48</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>c</entry>
      <entry>10</entry>
      <entry>40</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Find the product in Row a. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 49</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Find the product in Row b. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>96</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Find the product in Row c. </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>400</para>
<para>Use the following table to answer questions 2 – 5.</para>
<para>Here are some lengths and widths of a rectangle whose perimeter is 20 meters.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Row</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Length (meters)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Width (meters)</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Area (square meters)</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>a</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>9</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>b</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
      <entry>7</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>c</entry>
      <entry>5</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>d</entry>
      <entry>7</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>e</entry>
      <entry>9</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>Complete the <emphasis>Width</emphasis> column of the table.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Width in Row c </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 5</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Width in Row d </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Width in Row e </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>Complete the <emphasis>Area</emphasis> column of the table. What do you notice about the areas?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Area in Row a </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>9</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Area in Row b </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>21</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Area in Row c </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 25</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item> Area in Row d </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 21</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item> Area in Row e </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>9</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Without calculating, predict whether the area of the rectangle will be greater than or less than 25 square meters if the length is 5.25 meters.
    <list>
      <item> greater than </item>
      <item> less than </item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>less than</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>Plot the points for length and area from your table. Do the values change in a linear way? Do they change in an exponential way?
    <list>
      <item> linear </item>
      <item> exponential </item>
      <item> linear and exponential </item>
      <item> not linear and not exponential </item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> not linear and not exponential</para>
<para>Use the following scenario to answer questions 6 – 8.</para>
<para>Copies of a book are arranged in a stack. Each copy of a book is 2.1 cm thick.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Row</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Copies of book</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Stack height in cm</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>a</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>b</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>c</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>d</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>e</entry>
      <entry>4</entry>
      <entry> </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>Complete the table.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
    <item> Stack height in Row a </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>0</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
    <item> Stack height in Row b </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 2.1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
    <item> Stack height in Row c </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>4.2</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
    <item> Stack height in Row d </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>6.3</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
    <item> Stack height in Row e </item>
  </list>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 8.4</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>What is the difference in the height of the stack of books when a new copy of the book is added?</item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>2.1</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>How high is a stack of \(b\) books, in centimeters?
    <list>
      <item> \((2.1)b\) </item>
      <item> \(2.1 +b\) </item>
      <item> \(2.1(b-1)\) </item>
      <item> \(2.1^b\) </item>
    </list>
  </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \((2.1)b\)</para></section>
</content>
